# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE (steps/defects.md): a3 is declared after User, so in User's code a3 is no lexical
# declaration but a free dynamic input (docs #declaration-visibility, #dynamic): its coordinates are those of the
# declaration reaching it, Model (a3 is a merge of one Structure; l2_anchor_close), and its value is admitted to them
# where u1's execution forms the input -- the root's a3, the caller's binding.  C, the copy of the unit u1 hangs
# under, holds no a3 (made after the merge) and needs none.  Natively and with the root walked; the methods-walked twin
# is an implementation gap (walked code in a merge copy holds its coordinate witness as a copied frame operand).
# Exit 7; 81 if u1 read anything but a3's 1.
Model:
    int: x 1
end: Model
User:
    int: y 0
    y: a3\x
end: User
u1: merge: User
a3: merge: Model
u1
int: ok 7
if: u1\y != 1
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
